    "Baku Bakı and Russian Баку refer to one city, and 1918-09-17 government arrival from Ganja does not constitute a city-name change.",
    "Caucasus' continental classification is geographically variable; countries' modern ISO codes do not imply that the cities are legally or historically within a single defined continent.",
    "First 1801 timeline entries denote the beginning of Korean editorial survey, not documentary evidence that modern Korean transliterations were already used in 1801.",
    "All UI-facing summary/name notes are <=28 Unicode codepoints; expanded researchNote/researchDetail preserves full evidence.",
    "This is reviewed staging only; no PLAC v2 runtime tile, live map manifest, or main branch updated."
